1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
I don’t let AI
grade its own code.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,000
One request. A disposable cart.
Add a clear help example.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Start needs my Touch ID.
Bound to this exact request.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,000
No internet. Secrets blocked.
Every protected file that exists: denied (74 of 74).

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Five old tests still pass.
New behavior is not independently proved.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The Builder can’t read
or change the judge.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
New tests only count if they fail
on old code and pass on new code.

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,000
13 planted cheats. 0 passed.
6 failed. 7 inconclusive.

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Original tests were restored.
A fake passing test did not win.

10
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Ready for review. Not checked.
Accept stays locked.

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,000
One help-text change.
No Accept or Reject was pressed.

12
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,000
This verdict is signed
by my Mac’s security chip.

13
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Recorded evidence: control 13 before/after.

14
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:59,000
AI does the work.
It never grades itself.
